meta {
  name: Create Item
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/items
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "title": "My Item",
    "projectId": "{{projectId}}",
    "workphaseId": "{{workphaseId}}",
    "parentId": null
  }
}

docs {
  # Create Item

  Name the item's `projectId`, its `parentId`, or both; with neither it's a
  400. A `parentId` alone makes a child in the parent's project, and a
  `projectId` other than the parent's is a 400.

  A top-level item's attachment flag is clear, and `isAttached: true`
  without a `parentId` is a 400. A child is created attached unless
  `isAttached: false`.

  `workphaseId` is optional; omitted, a top-level item has none and shows in
  Unsorted. An attached child takes its parent's workphase, and naming
  another is a 400. A detached child that omits it takes the workphase its
  parent is shown in (a 400 if that has none). A Free item's workphase must
  belong to the workflow its project uses.

  See wiki item-attachment §1, §2a, §14.
}
